      "notes": "Agency: A&B Inmobiliaria. Urbanización Saltamonte, Loma del Escobero (near City Plaza / Euro del Escobero / Hospital Uribe Angel). Estrato 5.\n\n110 m2, 3 alcobas, 2 banos, TWO parking spaces, piso 1. Ground floor of the tower, but the building sits on the Escobero hillside, so the listing photos still show a LARGE brick-paved terrace with a full valley view — correcting my earlier assumption that piso 1 meant no view. And no elevator wait every time the dog needs out. Sala-comedor, cocina integral WITH DISHWASHER, estudio, zona de ropas, master with ensuite + vestier. Wood laminate in the bedrooms, delivered empty and freshly painted.\n\nBuilding: 24h security, visitor parking, salon social, pool, sauna, turco, elevator, gym, sports zone, playground, green areas, and PET ZONES — the listing says so explicitly, which is why this one is marked pets-ok and the Poblado one is not.\n\nCONFIRMED 15 Aug: 4.6M INCLUDES administracion, and dogs are allowed. That puts it just 100k over the 4.5M cap — effectively on budget.\n\nSTILL ASK A&B: furnished or not, and the available date.\n\nWALKABILITY, for contrast: Supermercado La Paz 248m and only ~30m below. Envigado's plaza de mercado and La Vaquita are ~915m away and only ~25m below - essentially flat. City Plaza mall (Cinepolis, Bodytech) is 681m but ~59m ABOVE, so you climb going and come back down carrying. This is the one that actually walks.",
