      "notes": "5.000.000/mo ALL IN — Jordan confirmed 15 Aug that this includes administracion, and that dogs are allowed. So 5.0M is the real number, 500k over the 4.5M cap.\n\nFrom the photos: big wraparound terrace with a real valley view, floor-to-ceiling sliders off the living room, proper zona de ropas (Bosch gas heater + sink), compact black-granite kitchen with gas cooktop, oven and a slatted island bar, master bath with double vanity + glass shower, second bath smaller. Interior is heavily styled: 3D geometric wallpaper on several walls, faux-stone accent wall, crystal chandeliers, mirrored wall. Not neutral — you'd be living inside someone's taste.\n\n98 m2 with a terrace that big means the indoor half is tight for 3BR+2BA. Bedrooms in the photos are modest.\n\nAmenities: heated adult + kids pool, sauna, turco, kids park + game room, sports field, walking trails, salon social.\n\nWHAT'S ACTUALLY WALKABLE (re-scanned 15 Aug from a corrected pin): Minimercado Espana 158m, Mall El Indio / D1 / Maxioferta ~340-370m, Origin Cafe 393m, Crepes & Waffles 820m, BFit 892m, Premium Plaza + Jumbo + Bodytech ~940-970m. So there IS a cluster.\n\nTHE CATCH IS VERTICAL. The building sits at ~1626m and everything is BELOW it: D1 and Mall El Indio are ~80-95m down, Jumbo/Premium Plaza ~145m down. Coming back from the D1 with bags is roughly a 25-story climb; from Jumbo it's ~145m of ascent over 950m, about a 15% grade. Elevation cross-checked against two datasets (ASTER30m and SRTM30m).",
